When most people think about getting a business website built, they assume a process that takes weeks — briefing sessions, design revisions, rounds of feedback, development, and then launch. For a fully custom, bespoke website, that's often accurate.

But for a managed starter website, the timeline is very different. Most are live within five to seven working days of receiving the information we need.

Here's how that's possible — and what you need to have ready to make it happen.

## Why Managed Starter Websites Can Be Built Quickly

The speed comes from a combination of factors that remove the bottlenecks that slow down traditional web design projects.

### AI-Assisted Building

Our managed starter websites use a streamlined build process without compromising on quality. Rather than dragging the project out for weeks, we gather the right details upfront, create a strong initial result quickly, then refine and tailor it to your business.

This isn't about using a generic template and swapping in your logo. It's about using modern tooling to produce a professional, properly structured website in significantly less time than a fully manual build would allow — keeping costs low and turnaround times fast.

### A Streamlined Process

Custom web design projects involve extensive back-and-forth: multiple design concepts, revisions, client approvals at each stage, and custom development work. A managed starter website has a more defined structure — we know what a well-built local business website needs, and we build it efficiently.

That doesn't mean the result is generic. It means the process is efficient.

### You Provide the Essentials, We Handle the Rest

The main variable in how quickly a managed website goes live is how quickly we receive the information we need from you. This is typically:

- Your business name, contact details, and location
- A description of your services
- Any photos of your work (these make a significant difference to quality)
- Any specific pages or information you want included

With this in hand, we can move quickly. Without it, even the fastest process stalls.

## What the Timeline Looks Like

**Day 1–2:** We receive your details and begin the build.

**Day 3–4:** A draft version is ready for your review. We share it with you and ask for any feedback.

**Day 5–7:** Any revisions are made and the site goes live on your domain.

The exact timing depends on how quickly feedback comes back. Businesses that review promptly and with clear notes tend to be live fastest.

## What You Get at the End

A managed starter website that's live in under a week isn't a rushed compromise — it's a professionally built site with:

- Clean, modern design
- Mobile-responsive layout
- SSL certificate and fast hosting
- SEO foundations in place
- Your contact information, services, and location clearly presented
- A working contact form

For more on what to expect once the site is live, see [what to expect in the first 3 months of your new website](/blog/what-to-expect-in-the-first-3-months-of-your-new-website/).

## Is a Quick Build Right for You?

If you need a professional website online quickly — you've just started a business, you've been operating without a site, or you want to stop losing customers to competitors who are more visible online — a managed starter website is an efficient route to a proper result.

[Get in touch](/contact/) and we'll let you know exactly what we'd need from you and how quickly your site could be live. Our [managed starter website service](/services/managed-starter-websites/) is designed to get quality results delivered fast.
